-- The Kling V3 Motion Control app of Fash's Apps menu, on fal: a character image plus a reference video, whose movements the output copies. Both modes
-- (Pro and Standard) take the same input schema (read 2026-10-26): image_url, video_url, character_orientation and keep_original_sound, with no ratio
-- or duration field, so the output follows the reference video and lasts as long as it. packages/core/src/providers/fal.ts sends orientation 'video'
-- (the reference may then run up to 30 s; 'image' allows 10 s) and no sound. The ratio is therefore 'auto', the durations are the whole seconds 3 to 30
-- (the job's duration is the reference video's, rounded up), and the 2 inputs are the image and the video. fal bills output seconds: $0.168 Pro and
-- $0.126 Standard (endpointBilling on the model pages). The output resolution is not stated; 720p is the floor the worker checks. Added disabled.
